  "elements": [
    "horizontal axis 'Distance (ft)' from 0 to 600 with ticks every 100",
    "vertical axis 'Height (ft)' with labeled ticks at 100, 200, 300",
    "faint dotted gridlines across the plotting area",
    "teal downward-opening parabolic trajectory starting at (0,0), peaking near (290,155), landing near (560,0)",
    "small teal arrowheads spaced along the curve indicating direction of travel",
    "small circular marker on the rising branch near (200,140)",
    "leader line + label 'Position of hitter' pointing to the origin",
    "leader line + label 'Trajectory of ball' pointing to the circular marker",
    "short red rectangle standing on the x-axis at 400 ft labeled 'Outfield wall'",
    "moving distance marker with a vertical drop line to the x-axis and a height readout",
    "highlight indicating whether the ball is above or below the wall at the wall's distance"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "distanceSlider",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Distance from hitter (ft)",
      "range": [
        0,
        560,
        5
      ],
      "default": 200,
      "teaches": "Each horizontal distance corresponds to exactly one height on the arc, so the trajectory is a function height(distance); dragging the marker makes the (distance, height) pair and the vertical drop to the ground concrete."
